// c-collection-03: the node-walk's collection firing rule drifted from the
// JIT's. MapQ fires on a resize only when its source fired, and MapQ and
// FoldQ fire on a source back from bottom only when it fired; the JIT loop
// (scaffold::SlotFlags) fires on either, as design/organic_firing.md says
// ("iff resized, or a slot fired, ...; a bottom source forgets the length,
// so the source's return is a resize").
//
// command: graphix-fuzz check design/review-2026-10-05/repro/c-collection-03.gx
//
// xs shrinks from [1, 2, 3] to [1] at n=3 while the map's arm sleeps. Arm 0
// reads xs, so the fire is not re-raised at the wake (n=4) and the map sees
// a STALE source of a new length. MapQ::update (collection.rs:1064) merges
// the source's STALE tag on the resize, so the map does not fire and `~`
// keeps its pre-sleep sample; the fused map loop fires.
//
// expected: Trace([0:i64:0 2:i64:-97 3:i64:-99 4:i64:4]) in every mode.
// observed: DIVERGENCE — fusion/JIT bug (interp != jit)
//   interp: Trace([0:i64:0 2:i64:-97 3:i64:-99 4:i64:0])
//   jit: Trace([0:i64:0 2:i64:-97 3:i64:-99 4:i64:4])
// With `array::fold(xs, 0, |acc, x| x) ~ n` in arm 1 both engines give 4:4
// (FoldQ fires on any resize).
//
// Back from bottom at the same length diverges for map AND fold (FoldQ
// requires `src_trig && back`, collection.rs:1522): k = uniq(select n
// { 0 => 0, 1 => 1, 2 => 1, 3 => 2, _ => 2 }), xs = select k { 0 => [1, 2, 3],
// 1 => never(), _ => [1, 2, 3] }: interp Trace([0:i64:0 3:i64:-97 4:i64:0]),
// jit Trace([0:i64:0 3:i64:-97 4:i64:4]), with either callback.
//
// An empty source at the arm's first selection also diverges for map (the
// early return at collection.rs:1069 takes the source's tag alone): s =
// uniq(select n { 0 => 0, 1 => 0, _ => 1 }), let xs: Array<i64> = []:
// interp Trace([0:i64:-100]), jit Trace([0:i64:-100 2:i64:2]).
let n = 0;
n <- select n { 8 => never(), v => v + 1 };
let k = uniq(select n { 0 => 0, 1 => 0, 2 => 0, 3 => 2, _ => 2 });
let s = uniq(select n { 0 => 1, 1 => 1, 2 => 0, 3 => 0, _ => 1 });
let xs = select k { 0 => [1, 2, 3], _ => [1] };
select s {
  0 => array::len(xs) - 100,
  _ => array::map(xs, |x| x) ~ n
}
